cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Synthesizer: a clean-room reimplementation of Pragna (POPL'10 + PLDI'11)"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Srivastava
    given-names: Saurabh
    email: s@saurabh-srivastava.com
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/saurabh-srivastava/code-synth"
abstract: >-
  A proof-theoretic synthesizer (predicate-abstraction over
  VS3-PA) that consumes (control-flow template, predicate
  space, English spec) and produces (code, proof).  Source
  emitters for Python, C, and Rust; Z3 + Lean dual
  verification backends.  Clean-room reimplementation of the
  Pragna synthesis line (POPL'10 + PLDI'11).
keywords:
  - program-synthesis
  - verification
  - predicate-abstraction
  - lean4
  - z3
  - vs3-pa
